# agentic-loop worker keys — copy to .env and fill in what you have.
# .env is gitignored. Scripts read this file from the project directory;
# keys are NEVER exported into your interactive Claude Code session.
#
# CRITICAL: never add an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY line here or export one in your
# shell. If ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, Claude Code bills your interactive
# session to the API instead of your Max subscription.

# Fable 5 worker — Claude API key, metered per token (separate from Max).
# Deliberately NOT named ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (see above).
FABLE_KEY=

# Sol (GPT-5.6) worker — OpenAI API key. Funds the DIRECT transport
# (call_sol.sh with no --via, the default) and is the only way to get
# --effort ultra, which needs the Responses multi-agent beta.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Cheap bulk workers — OpenRouter key. ALSO funds Sol as an alternate
# transport: `call_sol.sh --via openrouter` sends the identical prompts and
# envelope to openai/gpt-5.6-sol on OpenRouter, billed to this key instead,
# and reports OpenRouter's own figure rather than an estimate.
#   `--batch` (OpenRouter only) selects the :batch model id. Opt-in on
#   purpose: batch is NOT reliably cheaper — on 2026-08-07 z-ai/glm-5.2:batch
#   was priced above its own non-batch variant. Compare before using it.
# Transport is never inferred from which keys are present: adding this key
# does not move your Sol billing. Both transports stay metered, so the
# no-unattended-metered-calls rule applies to each of them unchanged.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Local model for call_ollama.sh. SET THIS — the shim's built-in fallback
# (qwen3.5:4b) is 4B-class, and every 4B-class model measured so far spends
# its whole budget inside <think> and returns an empty result the shim
# correctly reports as "partial": a wasted call that reads like a broken
# tier. Observed directly: qwen3.5:4b -> partial (3494 output tokens, no
# usable result), gemma4:12b -> ok (~400). doctor.sh warns if this resolves
# to a 4B-class model or one you have not pulled.
OLLAMA_MODEL=gemma4:12b

# Optional: override OpenRouter model aliases if the defaults go stale.
# These are model ids on a catalog that retires entries — verify a default
# still resolves at https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models before blaming the
# shim. `mimo` pointed at a delisted id (xiaomi/mimo-v2) until 2026-08-07.
# OPENROUTER_MODEL_KIMI=moonshotai/kimi-k2
# OPENROUTER_MODEL_MINIMAX=minimax/minimax-m2
# OPENROUTER_MODEL_MIMO=xiaomi/mimo-v2.5

# Pre-flight cost gate (scripts/lib/common.sh). Every metered shim prints an
# estimated cost to stderr BEFORE issuing its request, and refuses above this
# threshold unless the call is explicitly authorized. The estimate is an
# approximation (chars/4 for input, a declared assumed output that scales with
# --effort) and is NEVER written to the envelope's usage.est_cost_usd, which
# stays reserved for what a provider actually reported.
#   unset      -> the documented default, 1.00 USD
#   a number   -> that threshold, in USD. 0 means literally zero: refuse every
#                 metered call. It is NOT a way to disable the gate.
#   off        -> disable the refusal. The estimate is still printed.
#   anything else (empty, negative, non-numeric) -> refuse. A threshold that
#                 cannot be read must not be treated as "no limit".
# FACTORY_COST_THRESHOLD_USD=1.00
#
# Explicit authorization past the gate, for a call you have decided to make.
# Never inferred from a TTY or an interactive session — the unattended path is
# the one nobody is watching. Per-call: pass --authorize-cost instead.
# FACTORY_COST_AUTHORIZED=1
#
# Prices come from a committed table, not a live lookup (a network round-trip
# before every call trades cost for latency and a new failure mode). A model
# with no entry REFUSES rather than being treated as free — see
# preflight_price() in scripts/lib/common.sh to add one.

# Factory usage gate (scripts/lib/usage_gate.sh): postpone unattended loop
# iterations when subscription usage crosses the threshold (percent of the
# 5-hour or 7-day cap, from the statusline mirror in .agentic/usage.json).
# FACTORY_USAGE_THRESHOLD=90
# FACTORY_USAGE_STALE_MINUTES=120
# FACTORY_SPECS_DIR=factory/specs

# Observability export stack (scripts/observe_push.sh, opt-in — also needs
# `/agentic-loop:config observability stack on`). Points at the OpenObserve
# store over your tailnet; see templates/observability/README.md.
# O2_URL=https://<store-machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net
# O2_AUTH=you@example.com:your-openobserve-password
# O2_ORG=default
# O2_STREAM=agentic
